  "steps": [
    "Heat the oil in a large heavy-based saucepan, then add the garlic, chilli and onion. Fry for 2–3 minutes until beginning to soften.",
    "Add the thyme leaves and spices with a splash of water to prevent scorching. Fry for a further 2–3 minutes.",
    "Add the chickpeas and stock, season well, cover and cook for 10–15 minutes until the sauce has thickened.",
    "Optionally use a stick blender to mash up some of the curry for a thicker texture, or remove a small amount and mash with a fork before stirring it back in.",
    "Sprinkle with coriander if using, and serve."
  ],
  "notes": "Best served with roti or flatbread for scooping. Inspired by the Caribbean flavours of Trinidad."
}
